{"name":"Metropolitan Silhouette","hex":"#3e4244","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"metropolitan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bishop empowered to oversee other bishops; an archbishop. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The inhabitant of a metropolis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to the see or province of a metropolitan.","Of, or pertaining to, a metropolis or other large urban settlement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metropolitan"},{"term":"silhouette","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artistic depiction, often of a person's profile, in the form of an outline without any other visual details, similar to a shadow, made by cutting a piece of black paper, filling in an outline with a solid colour (usually black), etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A dark outline of someone or something seen against a brighter background."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Often followed by against or upon: to depict (oneself or someone, or something) as a silhouette (noun sense 1 or noun sense 2.1); to project (oneself or someone, or something) upon a background, so as to be like a silhouette.","To appear as a silhouette."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silhouette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silhouette","blocks":[{"text":"A silhouette is the image of a person, animal, object or scene represented as a solid shape of a single colour, usually black, with its edges matching the outline of the subject. The interior of a silhouette is featureless, and the silhouette is usually presented on a light background, usually white, or none at all. The silhouette differs from an outline, which depicts the edge of an object in a linear form, while a silhouette appears as a solid shape. Silhouette images may be created in any visual artistic medium, but were first used to describe pieces of cut paper, which were then stuck to a backing in a contrasting colour, and often framed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/WALDST3.jpg/330px-WALDST3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silhouette","wikidata":"Q898700"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/GoetheVorEinemGrabmalMitWeiblicherBuesteS92.jpg/500px-GoetheVorEinemGrabmalMitWeiblicherBuesteS92.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/GoetheVorEinemGrabmalMitWeiblicherBuesteS92.jpg/500px-GoetheVorEinemGrabmalMitWeiblicherBuesteS92.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Goethe facing a grave monument, cut paper, 1780","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoetheVorEinemGrabmalMitWeiblicherBuesteS92.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Corinthian_pyxis_6th_c._BC_Antikenmuseum_Basel_n1.jpg/500px-Corinthian_pyxis_6th_c._BC_Antikenmuseum_Basel_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Corinthian_pyxis_6th_c._BC_Antikenmuseum_Basel_n1.jpg/1280px-Corinthian_pyxis_6th_c._BC_Antikenmuseum_Basel_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Corinthian_pyxis_6th_c._BC_Antikenmuseum_Basel_n1.jpg/500px-Corinthian_pyxis_6th_c._BC_Antikenmuseum_Basel_n1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Corinthian black-figure pyxis, 6th century BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACorinthian_pyxis_6th_c._BC_Antikenmuseum_Basel_n1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Terracotta_Panathenaic_prize_amphora_MET_GR147.jpg/330px-Terracotta_Panathenaic_prize_amphora_MET_GR147.jpg?utm_source=en.w